QF9700 driver source bundled for offline installation
====================================================

Upstream project:
  https://github.com/pgquiles/qf9700
  Linux driver for the Genoa Systems QF9700 USB2NET network adapter.
  Original author: jokeliujl <jokeliu@163.com> (2010-10-01), GPLv2.

What is bundled here:
  qf9700.c   - driver source (patched for modern kernels, see header)
  qf9700.h   - register definitions (unchanged from upstream)
  Makefile   - builds qf9700.ko against /lib/modules/$(uname -r)/build
  dkms.conf  - optional DKMS registration (version 1.0)

Patches vs upstream pgquiles/qf9700:
  1. USB IDs: upstream only claims 0fe6:9700.
     This bundle also claims 0fe6:9702 on USB interface 1 via:
       USB_DEVICE_INTERFACE_NUMBER(0x0fe6, 0x9702, 1)
     Reason: 9702 is a composite device. Interface 0 is a fake
     USB-storage CD-ROM (Windows drivers), interface 1 is the real
     Ethernet function. Without the interface-number match the driver
     never binds on 9702. (Same fix as genocem/bzapal forks.)
  2. Modern kernel build (5.15 / 6.x, Ubuntu 22.04 GA + HWE):
     - removed .get_settings/.set_settings from ethtool_ops
       (removed from struct ethtool_ops since 4.x)
     - .ndo_eth_ioctl on >= 5.15, .ndo_do_ioctl on older kernels
     - eth_hw_addr_set() on >= 5.17, memcpy(dev_addr) fallback older
     - FLAG_LINK_INTR, supports_autosuspend, dev_dbg(), mdelay()
  3. No functional change to MAC/PHY register logic (NCR/PAR/MAR/PRR,
     QF_RD_REGS/QF_WR_REGS, rx_fixup/tx_fixup framing).

Build (on target, offline):
  cd driver/qf9700
  make
  # produces qf9700.ko

Install is handled by ../../install.sh:
  - copies qf9700.ko to /lib/modules/<kver>/kernel/drivers/net/usb/
  - depmod -a, modprobe qf9700
  - installs usb-storage quirk for 9702 (options usb-storage quirks=0fe6:9702:i)
  - installs modules-load.d + udev rule, optional DKMS if dkms is present

References for 9702 composite behaviour:
  - https://github.com/genocem/usb-2-10-100m-ethernet-adapter-rd9700-updated-linux-driver
  - AskUbuntu "VK-QF9700 0fe6:9702" (usb-devices shows If#0 stor. + If#1 (none))

License: GPLv2 (see ../../LICENSE, original notices retained).
